I've been working on a "thievery" patch which turns lock-picking into a
skill with varying availability based on class. Locks have a difficulty
rating based on the depth of the level at which they are created.
Failing to pick a lock may jam it. Skeleton keys become significantly
rarer and more valuable - you don't need to be skilled to use them.

The idea of the patch is to promote class-distinctions. If your class
doesn't have thieving skills, then you'll need to look to other
alternatives: wands, knock spells or just kicking the cr*p out of it.

